<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabrán mac Domangairt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 558</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabrán mac Domangairt was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> in the mid-6th century, said to be a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fergus-mor">Fergus Mór</a>. The Cenél nGabráin, rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kintyre">Kintyre</a> and later dominant in Dál Riata, took their name from him, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a> became the kingdom's most powerful ruler. The Irish annals record his death around 558, close to a flight before the Pictish king Bridei.</p></div>
